      "statusChangeNewStatus": "closed",
      "value": "This is how it's supposed to work. In VR, it uses the original location of the camera as the root of your playspace, and it offsets the position and rotation of the camera to where you are within your playspace. This does makes certain use cases more difficult, but it is behaving exactly how it should nonetheless.",
