  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-03-12T21:25:08.504Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When using the camera component on an avatar to adjust were my view is on the fly (lets say a toggleable 3rd person cam for example) the camera will not display from the correct position in VR, on desktop its just fine, but in VR I've had it randomly position its self anywhere between close to the avatar in the wrong spot to way up in the air, sometimes even at an angle I never set.\n\nwhen trying to apply the camera to a bone by moving it in the hierarchy, the camera will fly hundreds of feet in the air, and you wont be able to see whats going on\n\nwhen you have the camera attached to the base of the avatar and either leave it be or use a constraint to bind it to a bone/object, the camera will be much closer than the former but it will still be in the wrong spot, change randomly on reuploads, and can even be rotated incorrectly\n\nin desktop mode, both methods of attaching the camera to an object work as expected, this bug merely effects VR only",
